APPROACH — COMPOSE THE CANONICAL COMPONENTS (not a re-implementation)
  The web page composes <TripReplayMap> + <TripReplayCharts>. The P4 component
  library already ships their native ports as page-fed surfaces:
    - TeslaSync/feature-views/TripReplayMap.*    (TripReplayMap / TripReplayMapModel /
      TripReplayMapSource / TripReplayPosition / TripReplaySpeedBand)
    - TeslaSync/feature-views/TripReplayCharts.* (TripReplayCharts / TripReplayChartsModel /
      TripReplayChartsSource / TripReplayPoint / TripReplayFormat / TripReplayPhase)
    - shared-surfaces/PlaybackSpeedMenu.*        (PlaybackSpeedMenu / ReplaySpeed)
  Their models are explicitly designed as "controlled children fed by the page"
  (single source of truth, web `onSeekToIndex`). So the page COMPOSES them:
    * TripReplayPageModel owns the drive + the replay clock + `currentIndex`.
    * Two page-owned bridges (TripReplayPageMapBridge / …ChartsBridge) publish the
      page snapshot into each surface and route seeks back to the page model, so
      the map marker, the chart playhead, the scrubber and the stat bar stay in
      lockstep — exactly the web "single source of truth" contract.
  Shared value types (TripReplayPosition / TripReplayPoint / ReplaySpeed /
  TripReplayFormat / TripReplayPhase) are REUSED, never re-declared (DRY). My
  page-level types are uniquely named (TripReplayPageModel/Status/Format, …);
  a full collision scan confirmed only `TripReplayPhase`+`TripReplayFormat`
  overlapped the component library, so the page enum is `TripReplayPageStatus`
  and the page formatters are `TripReplayPageFormat`.

